{
  "description": "SASRec encodes interaction histories using item and learned positional embeddings, causal self-attention, and feed-forward blocks. It scores candidates by dot product with the final sequence representation, sharing input/output item embeddings. Training uses next-item supervision and sampled binary cross-entropy. Source: [Self-Attentive Sequential Recommendation](https://arxiv.org/html/1808.09781).",
  "motivation": "Attention adaptively selects relevant past interactions, balancing recent transitions with longer-range preferences. Despite the supplied title, SASRec is not a dedicated cold-start solution: its learned item embeddings depend on observed interactions.",
  "implementation_notes": "Start from RecHarness sasrec_perdataset and retain Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, CDs_and_Vinyl and dataset routing. Keep preprocessing seed=0, training seed=42, DATA_DIR=os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and the SASREC_EPOCHS environment default of 200. Select using macro validation HR@10 under the pinned evaluator; no matched-task improvement is established by the paper. Preserve splits and store artifacts beneath the trial directory. Architecture changes must update the predictor writer and DiagnosisProbe(view, device).run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), returning metrics and metric_definitions. Use only observed data; ratings, review text, and simulator traits are unavailable.",
  "pseudocode": "for category in four_categories:\n    load unchanged training split\n    initialize category-specific SASRec\n    for epoch in configured_epochs:\n        for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n            features = model.log2feats(sequence)  # causal and padding masks\n            mask = positive != 0\n            pos_logits = dot(features, model.item_emb(positive))\n            neg_logits = dot(features, model.item_emb(negative))\n            loss = mean(softplus(-pos_logits[mask]) + softplus(neg_logits[mask]))\n            update parameters with Adam\n    save checkpoint and architecture configuration beneath trial directory\nwrite matching working/predict.py with category routing\nuse host validation macro HR@10 for trial selection",
  "originality": {
    "score": 2,
    "positive": "The paper introduced an influential attention-based approach to sequential recommendation.",
    "negative": "Relative to the required SASRec baseline, this description introduces no new mechanism. Scores use a subjective 1–10 scale."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "Available titles and descriptions could support a separately validated content-based extension for sparse items.",
    "negative": "Such an extension is not established here; true cold-start performance requires explicit evaluation."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "The existing SASRec baseline already supplies the main architecture and training path.",
    "negative": "Masking, checkpoint compatibility, predictor generation, and diagnostic adapters require care. Higher scores indicate greater difficulty."
  }
}
